{"id": "EUVD-2026-59219", "enisaUuid": "aa59b206-d4f4-3f4c-8c05-5b24beb15b2b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnetfilter: nft_lookup: fix catchall element handling with inverted lookups\n\nnft_lookup_eval() decides whether a lookup matched (`found`) from the\ndirect set lookup and priv->invert before falling back to the\ncatchall element used by interval sets (e.g. nft_set_rbtree) for the\nopen-ended default range. Since `found` is never recomputed after\n`ext` is replaced by the catchall lookup, inverted lookups\n(NFT_LOOKUP_F_INV, \"!= @set\") can wrongly match or wrongly skip the\ncatchall element, producing the wrong verdict. Fold the catchall\nlookup into `ext` before computing `found`, matching the order\nalready used by nft_objref_map_eval().", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:31", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65d35cb555f40529a9edc6bf4beaa3bee917f015", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0ab8880865f9678eb6174e72c1fc4712e44c745c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/238c612357b5a25f03eacf356f95034f8551f218", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef0c7d4b04a0e6ad175323c24bc84e11470dd79d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6107a4c74b54cb33e3bce162a63048ae5a6b198"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72320", "GHSA-xm9x-r949-vc7p"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.52, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c155fa4-5bdc-335a-b999-f6e4a4bbfdfc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "405ba2e9-be56-3ba6-a50c-a8b978105283", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "474b3dfe-50b6-3b54-bb6a-3ab40bd7c7dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa31047a6d25da0fa101da1ed544e1247949b40 <238c612357b5a25f03eacf356f95034f8551f218"}, {"id": "52709643-5cfa-3abf-9196-525d9ebb8de6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "5eec68a6-c4c8-3300-b7e5-d0d9a69b496d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "74122e21-d7c4-3bdb-b5cd-777334e49561", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa31047a6d25da0fa101da1ed544e1247949b40 <e6107a4c74b54cb33e3bce162a63048ae5a6b198"}, {"id": "884b74c8-7b6e-3742-9ec5-fa9ae00ef112", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "95742d71-4a93-3044-b74c-2a2611e8f5c1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa31047a6d25da0fa101da1ed544e1247949b40 <0ab8880865f9678eb6174e72c1fc4712e44c745c"}, {"id": "97ed2519-9843-326f-ac4e-1d6f4be02fcf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa31047a6d25da0fa101da1ed544e1247949b40 <65d35cb555f40529a9edc6bf4beaa3bee917f015"}, {"id": "ab011b9d-0e7b-3848-a186-26be6689b01f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "ad5ad995-5c22-348e-8ca6-a99e2ff24dce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aaa31047a6d25da0fa101da1ed544e1247949b40 <ef0c7d4b04a0e6ad175323c24bc84e11470dd79d"}, {"id": "f0ea065b-cee8-3031-ae0a-931c6c626083", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ac89d332-f156-36de-97a0-3d9d2703eb6c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}